# Normalise text to LF in the repo. Without this, cloning on Windows with core.autocrlf=true
# gives a CRLF working tree, and running those same files from WSL or Linux hands `\r` to bash:
# the shebang becomes `#!/bin/sh^M` and the script dies with "bad interpreter".
# Git Bash tolerates CRLF, so this only ever bites the WSL/Linux path - which is exactly the
# path that has no easy way to diagnose it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for everything that is executed rather than read.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
install.sh  text eol=lf
hooks/*     text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
